# Deliberately tracked, not ignored: dependencies.lock pins exact
# resolved component versions, and managed_components/ is the actual
# resolved source trees — both committed so a fresh CI checkout never
# needs to query the component registry at all. A lock file alone
# wasn't enough: the component manager still re-queries the registry
# for "latest matching" versions to validate the lock even when one is
# present, and that re-query hit a newly-published component manifest
# with "if:" syntax PlatformIO's bundled idf-component-manager can't
# parse — confirmed failing in CI with the lock file alone (the same
# underlying parser limitation already documented in
# src/idf_component.yml's esp_lcd_st77916 comment, just surfacing on a
# different dependency). Committing the resolved trees directly removes
# the network dependency entirely.
# dependencies.lock
# managed_components/

# build-time secrets — don't commit your real WiFi credentials
src/wifi_creds.h
